}

data srv4_memory_population_observation_note: String = "srv4 BMC 192.168.1.195 Redfish observation 2026-08-22, taken between 19:46Z and 20:15Z (the exact minute was not recorded at read time and is NOT reconstructed here -- the window is bounded below by the 19:45:57Z correctable-ECC entry this session read first and above by the srv3 read at 20:15:38Z). srv3 carries a precise timestamp because its read was taken against a live boot transition and the clock mattered; this one was not, and a fabricated second would be worth less than an honest window. Taken through the rotated credential in Secret Manager (bmc-srv4-admin) -- the authenticated read this host's deferral named as its dissolution condition, so that scaffold is RETIRED by this row rather than carried forward. MemorySummary TotalSystemMemoryGiB=512; per-DIMM dimm0..dimm7 ALL M393A8G40D40-CRB CapacityMiB=65536 OperatingSpeedMhz=2133 RankCount=2 Manufacturer=Samsung, eight distinct serials, banks DDR4_A1 through H1, every module State=Enabled Health=OK and system HealthRollup=OK.\n\nTHE DEFERRAL'S OWN INSTRUCTION SAID TO DECODE AGAINST THE SK HYNIX CATALOG AND THAT INSTRUCTION IS SUPERSEDED, which is worth saying because following it literally would have produced a wrong row. It was written when the expected finding was srv1's uniform Hynix population; what is actually installed is a Samsung part that had no catalog row at all until 2026-08-22. The deferral was right that srv1's population must not be assumed, and wrong about which catalog the answer would come from.\n\nONE CORRECTABLE ECC EVENT IS ON RECORD FOR THIS POPULATION, logged 2026-08-22T19:45:57Z on Socket 0 / Channel 0 / DIMM 0 (bank 13, row 166, column 96), about three minutes after an unclean restart following a power blackout. It was corrected by ECC and no uncorrectable event accompanied it. It is recorded here rather than left in the BMC log because it is the only memory event this population has produced and because a repeat at the same bank/row/column would distinguish a marginal device from a single upset -- see gunbc.host_memory_qualification for the qualification standing this does not by itself change."

data srv4_memory_population: HostMemoryPopulation = HostMemoryPopulation {
  rows: [
    MemoryPopulationRow { module: m393a8g40d40_crb0q_catalog, stick_count: 8 },
  ],
}

data srv4_host: ComputeHost = ComputeHost {
  identity: gunbc.fleet_intent_network.operator_host_srv4,
  baseboard: Present { value: srv4_baseboard },
  bmc_intent: Present { value: gunbc.bmc_intent.fleet_bmc_valid_state },
  processors: [CpuProcessor { cpu: fleet_intent_cpu }],
  memory: memory_devices_from_population(pop: srv4_memory_population),
  storage: [srv4_nvme0],
  network_interfaces: [],
}

data fleet_intent_known_hosts: List<ComputeHost> = [srv1_host, srv2_host, srv3_host, srv4_host]

fn fleet_intent_execution_surface() -> ExecutionSurface {
  ExecutionSurface {
    os: fleet_intent_os_surface,
    isolation: PerJobFilesystem,
    container_runtime: Present { value: Docker },
    toolchains: [extdeps.cache.sccache.sccache_toolchain_capability],
    mounted_storage: [],
    network: [],
  }
}
